tpc-fleet: multi-tenant TPC-B throughput across 5 nodes (one single-writer shard per tenant)
  sweep tenants=1024, 400 txns/tenant, 1000 accounts/tenant — aggregate txn/s + per-node split

  cross-LB warm SELECT 1 RTT p50: 198µs (the per-statement network floor)

  --- throughput vs tenant concurrency (one writer per tenant, no intra-shard convoy) ---
  tenants        txns       txn/s    p50 ms    p95 ms    p99 ms   errs  shed
  1024         409600      2785.6    147.12    446.31   1734.92  16848     0

  --- per-node distribution (the LB keyspace-partition carrying the throughput) ---
  node          shards      queries
  fathom1          197       553052
  fathom2          200       561444
  fathom3          186       522158
  fathom4          222       623323
  fathom5          219       614799

  fleet:  1024 tenant shards over 5 nodes (2874776 queries recorded), spread 1.19x (1.00 = perfect).
          Each tenant is one single-writer file on the node the LB hashed it to, so throughput
          partitions across the fleet with no cross-tenant contention (contrast the single-shard
          convoy in docs/reviews/tpc-run-2026-07-10.md). Absolute txn/s is CPU-bound by this one
          12-vCPU VM; on N separate machines the partitioned work is ~N× (the 'millions' angle).
